        title: "Introduction to Aryorithm",
        category: "getting-started",
        content: "Aryorithm Technologies provides deterministic, sub-millisecond active defense for sovereign infrastructure. Our platform integrates kernel-level packet inspection, industrial protocol dissection, physical constraint validation, and local AI inference into a single, cohesive defense system.\n\n## What Makes Aryorithm Different\n\nUnlike traditional SIEMs that generate alerts for human analysts, Aryorithm takes autonomous action. When it detects a threat, it mitigates at the kernel level in under one microsecond — before the packet reaches the TCP/IP stack, before the application layer, before any actuator can respond.\n\n## The Four Pillars\n\n1. **Zero Cloud Dependencies** — Every capability executes on the appliance. No control plane to phone home to, no model to fetch, no third-party script in the UI.\n\n2. **Deterministic Fast-Paths** — Critical inspection engineered strictly in C++20 and eBPF kernel space. Zero garbage collection pauses, zero Python in the execution hot-path.\n\n3. **Cryptographic Hardware Identity** — Zero-trust trust anchors rooted in physical TPM 2.0 cryptoprocessors rather than spoofable software certificates.\n\n4. **Data Sovereignty** — Enterprise site telemetry remains the exclusive, uncompromised property of the infrastructure owner.\n\n## Quick Start\n\nTo get started with Aryorithm, you will need:\n\n- A Blackbox Sentinel appliance (S-1000, S-5000, or V-Edge)\n- A network segment with at least one 10GbE connection\n- A workstation for the initial configuration\n\nThe standard deployment timeline is 10 business days from POC request to live appliance. This includes hardware shipping, air-gapped installation, protocol dissector configuration, and operator training.\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Read the Installation Guide to prepare your environment\n- Explore the Configuration Reference to understand available options\n- Review the Security Architecture to understand how Aryorithm protects your infrastructure",
