        slug: "quick-start",
        title: "Quick Start Guide",
        category: "getting-started",
        content: "This guide walks you through the initial setup of your Blackbox Sentinel appliance.\n\n## Step 1: Physical Installation\n\n1. Mount the appliance in your rack (1U or 2U)\n2. Connect power cables to both PSUs\n3. Connect the management network cable to the first 10GbE port\n4. Connect the mirror/SPAN port to the second 10GbE port\n5. Connect the console cable for initial configuration\n\n## Step 2: First Boot\n\n1. Power on the appliance\n2. Wait for the boot sequence to complete (approximately 3 minutes)\n3. Connect to the console port using a USB-C to RJ45 adapter\n4. Open a terminal emulator at 115200 baud\n5. Log in with the default credentials:\n   - Username: admin\n   - Password: (printed on the asset tag)\n\n## Step 3: Initial Configuration\n\nThe first-boot wizard will guide you through:\n\n1. **Network Configuration** — Set the management IP address, gateway, and DNS\n2. **Time Configuration** — Set the NTP server or configure PTP\n3. **Admin Password** — Change the default admin password\n4. **TPM Initialization** — Initialize the TPM 2.0 module and create the endorsement key\n5. **Protocol Selection** — Select which industrial protocol dissectors to enable\n\n## Step 4: Verify Operation\n\n1. Check the dashboard for system health\n2. Verify that the XDP fast-path is active\n3. Confirm that the selected protocol dissectors are loaded\n4. Run a test traffic replay to verify detection\n\n## Step 5: Connect to Sentinel Nexus (Optional)\n\nIf you have a Sentinel Nexus orchestration plane:\n\n1. Navigate to Fleet > Join Fleet\n2. Enter the Nexus appliance IP address\n3. Provide the fleet enrollment token\n4. Wait for attestation to complete\n\n## Next Steps\n\n- Configure your protocol dissectors\n- Set up physical constraint maps\n- Define alert thresholds and notification channels\n- Schedule your first training session",
